Author: Dmytro Surovtsev <xelth-com@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 26 17:10:03 2026 +0200

    0.5.0 candidate, wave 24: a timeout never loses the review; one truth about availability
    
    - Continuation: a reviewer killed on its timeout gets one continuation turn on the same thread
      (codex resume, agy conversation, muse session) with a finish-now prompt and -ContinueSec
      (default: the smaller of the timeout and 900 s); its reply is ingested like a first-turn reply
      (ledger timeout_continue); otherwise a partial reply is salvaged from the event stream into
      <NN>-<engine>-<slug>.partial.md and the exact resume command is printed. Verified live before
      coding: glm-5.3 resumed after an 1800 s kill and delivered a structured ACCEPT in 148 s.
    - Per-purpose default timeouts (checkpoint 900, framing/decision 1800, diff-review/core-contract/
      stuck 2400, acceptance 3600, chore 600), -TimeoutSec still wins; -Range <git range> for
      diff-review/acceptance with a size warning; F15-1: the muse billing guard re-reads auth.json
      before launch.
    - Availability: the providers listing, -Short (and -Short -Json), the SessionStart hook and the
      roster walk share one verdict per roster entry (Select-PanelMembers -NoNetwork); a usage limit
      without a reset time is out for exactly 60 minutes on every surface; LAST FAILURE shows any
      limit that still blocks; the listing names the ledger directory it read (the T2 disagreement was
      a listing run in another repository reading that repository's ledgers).
    
    Tests: new harness-visibility (76); full suite green under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (0.3 227,
    roster 117, format 37, engines 97, muse 72, panel 53, visibility 76, pending 26, fixes 45,
    lock2 11, 3b 12); roster, engines and visibility also under pwsh 7.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn8ZSCLGrVK4gD4UbcYhgZ

